{"lstm": "LSTM, or Long Short-Term Memory, is a specialized recurrent neural network designed to address the limitations of traditional RNNs, such as vanishing and exploding gradients. It effectively handles long-term dependencies in sequence data, making it highly useful for tasks like time series analysis and aimbot detection in games. LSTM's memory cells enable it to store information over extended periods, providing superior performance in sequence prediction tasks compared to other architectures like bidirectional GRU.|Here is another description: LSTM, or Long Short-Term Memory, is a type of recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture that is designed to better capture long-term dependencies and mitigate the vanishing gradient problem often encountered in traditional RNNs. It is particularly effective in sequence prediction tasks and has been applied in various domains including natural language processing and time series analysis.|Here is another description: LSTM, or Long Short-Term Memory, is a type of recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture designed to better capture long-term dependencies and mitigate issues like vanishing gradients, which are common in traditional RNNs. It is particularly effective in sequence prediction tasks and has been applied in various domains, including natural language processing and time-series analysis."},
