{"type_of_recurrent_neural_network": "A recurrent neural network (RNN) is a class of artificial neural networks where connections between nodes form a directed graph along a sequence. This allows it to exhibit temporal dynamic behavior, making it suitable for tasks involving sequential data like time series, natural language processing, and more."},
