{"model__used__seven_accuracy_threshold_values": "The model utilized seven distinct accuracy threshold values to determine the confidence level at which a prediction is classified as a true positive, aiming to balance the detection of aimbotting with minimizing false positives and negatives."},
{"seven_accuracy_threshold_values": "The seven accuracy threshold values used by the model are 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 0.95, and 0.99. These thresholds represent varying levels of confidence required for the model to classify a sample as aimbotting, with higher values indicating greater confidence needed for classification.|Here is another description: The subject refers to a set of seven specific values used as thresholds for determining the accuracy of a model in classifying samples as true positives for aimbotting behavior."},
