{"0_5_0_6_0_7_0_8_0_9_0_95_and_0_99": "The object consists of the seven accuracy threshold values\u20140.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 0.95, and 0.99\u2014which are used to determine the confidence level at which the model classifies predictions as true positives for aimbotting."},
{"false_positives_or_false_negatives": "False positives or false negatives refer to errors in classification where the system incorrectly identifies a sample. In the context of detecting aimbotting in gaming, these errors can lead to significant consequences for players."},
{"false_positives_or_false_negatives__mean__either_a_player_is_being_flagged_and_potentially_punished_for_an_offense_they_did_not_commit_or_the_player_committing_the_offense_is_not_being_caught_at_all": "The term \"mean\" in this context signifies the consequence or implication of having false positives or false negatives in the classification process. It highlights the potential outcomes that arise from these errors."},
