{"the_bidirectional_gru_network_on_our_dataset": "The object \"the bidirectional GRU network on our dataset\" describes the specific tool or method applied by the researchers. The bidirectional GRU network is a type of recurrent neural network that processes data in both forward and backward directions, and \"our dataset\" refers to the collection of data the researchers have compiled for their study on aimbotting detection."},
{"operators_and_players": "Operators and players are individuals or entities involved in the operation and participation within a gaming or network environment, where maintaining fair play and accurate detection systems are crucial."},
{"operators_and_players__reassurance__the_network_is_unlikely_to_falsely_flag_players_for_cheating": "Reassurance in this context refers to the confidence or certainty provided to operators and players regarding the reliability and accuracy of a detection system, specifically in identifying cheating without false positives."},
{"the_network_is_unlikely_to_falsely_flag_players_for_cheating": "The network is a system designed to detect cheating in games, specifically aimbotting, with high accuracy and confidence levels, ensuring it is unlikely to mistakenly flag legitimate players for cheating."},
{"network_inference_speed": "The network inference speed refers to the time it takes for the neural network to process input data and produce an output, which is crucial for real-time applications such as detecting cheating in online games."},
