{"30_dropout": "30% dropout is a regularization technique used in neural networks to prevent overfitting. It involves randomly setting a fraction (30% in this case) of the input units to 0 at each update during training time, which helps in reducing the interdependence of neurons and thus improving the network's generalization ability."},
