{"false_positives_or_false_negatives": "False positives or false negatives refer to errors in classification where the system incorrectly identifies a sample. In the context of detecting aimbotting in gaming, these errors can lead to significant consequences for players."},
{"false_positives_or_false_negatives__mean__either_a_player_is_being_flagged_and_potentially_punished_for_an_offense_they_did_not_commit_or_the_player_committing_the_offense_is_not_being_caught_at_all": "The term'mean' in this context signifies the consequence or implication of false positives or false negatives. It highlights the potential outcomes that arise from these classification errors in the system."},
