{"the_chosen_best_parameters": "The object \"the chosen best parameters\" represents the specific set of hyper-parameters that the researchers determined to be optimal for their LSTM model based on their manual search and empirical results.|Here is another description: The chosen best parameters refer to the optimal set of hyper-parameters selected for the LSTM model after a manual search based on intuition and empirical results. These parameters were fine-tuned to balance the complexity of the network with its ability to learn effectively.|Here is another description: The chosen best parameters refer to the optimal settings selected for the LSTM model's hyper-parameters after a manual search based on intuition and empirical results. These parameters were found to provide a balance in the model's complexity."},
{"the_chosen_best_parameters__gave__the_network_enough_complexity_to_learn_the_detailed_patterns_in_the_time_series": "The predicate \"gave\" in this context signifies that the selected parameters provided the necessary conditions for the LSTM network to function effectively. It indicates a cause-and-effect relationship where the parameters directly influenced the network's performance."},
{"the_network_enough_complexity_to_learn_the_detailed_patterns_in_the_time_series": "The network enough complexity to learn the detailed patterns in the time series refers to the LSTM model achieving a level of complexity that allowed it to capture and understand the intricate patterns present in the time series data. This complexity was crucial for the model to perform proper classification."},
{"the_chosen_best_parameters__were_not__too_complex_as_to_hinder_learning": "The phrase \"were not\" indicates a condition where the chosen parameters did not exceed a certain level of complexity. This suggests that the parameters were carefully selected to avoid overcomplicating the model."},
{"too_complex_as_to_hinder_learning": "The object \"too complex as to hinder learning\" describes a state where the model's complexity could negatively impact its ability to learn from the data. The chosen parameters were thus selected to prevent this from happening."},
{"table_2": "Table 2 is a part of the document that presents specific data related to the performance of different models under various conditions.|Here is another description: Table 2 is a data presentation format within a document that organizes information in a structured manner, allowing for easy comparison and analysis of different data points."},
