{"classification_accuracies": "Classification accuracies refer to the percentage of correct predictions made by a model. In this context, they are specifically measured for a test set using various confidence thresholds.|Here is another description: Classification accuracies refer to the measures of how well a model correctly identifies instances in a given dataset. In this context, they are specifically the results obtained from evaluating the performance of LSTM and GRU networks.|Here is another description: Classification accuracies refer to the effectiveness of a model in correctly categorizing data points into predefined classes. In the context of the provided table, these accuracies are measured for a test set using specific network architectures."},
