{"gettargetblock_from_the_livingentity_class": "The object `getTargetBlock from the LivingEntity class` refers to a specific method within the Minecraft server software. This method is part of the `LivingEntity` class, which is a parent class to the `Player` class. The `getTargetBlock` method is used to retrieve the block that a living entity, such as a player, is targeting, providing the coordinates `target_x`, `target_y`, and `target_z`."},
{"we__turned_our_focus_to__aimbotting": "The predicate \"turned our focus to\" indicates a shift in the researchers' attention or concentration from a broader topic to a specific area of interest within that topic. In this case, it signifies the researchers' decision to concentrate their efforts on studying aimbotting in the context of online games."},
{"accel_yaw_accel_pitch": "`accel_yaw` and `accel_pitch` are features representing the acceleration in yaw and pitch angles, respectively, which are crucial for detecting aimbot usage in Minecraft. These features are part of the player information that can be captured using the plugin API of a Minecraft server."},
