{"the_popular_recurrent_neural_network_architecture_long_short_term_memory": "The object \"the popular recurrent neural network architecture Long Short-Term Memory\" refers to a type of neural network known for its effectiveness in processing sequential data. Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks are a variant of recurrent neural networks (RNNs) that are designed to better capture long-term dependencies and are widely used in various applications involving time series data, such as speech recognition, language modeling, and, as in this context, detecting cheating behaviors in online games."},
